<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <style>
        /*
         * One family for the whole document. The website stack is
         * 'Inter', "Segoe UI", system-ui, -apple-system, sans-serif (public/assets/css/app.css),
         * none of which dompdf can load — it only ships DejaVu Sans, Helvetica, Times and
         * Courier. DejaVu Sans is the humanist sans closest to Inter and the only bundled
         * family with full Unicode coverage, so it stands in for the web font here.
         *
         * Do NOT use font-weight values other than normal/bold in PDF templates:
         * dompdf's FontMetrics::getType() maps 700 to "bold" but leaves 800/900 as the
         * literal subtype "800"/"900", which no bundled family declares, so the lookup
         * misses and dompdf silently falls back to its default serif (Times) — that was
         * the serif/sans mix on invoices and packing slips.
         */
        body {
            font-family: 'DejaVu Sans', Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif;
            font-size: 9px;
            line-height: 1.35;
            color: #1e293b;
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
        }
        @page {
            margin: 0.8cm;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    {% block admin_body %}{% endblock %}
</body>
</html>
